WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.538
Now the honest limits.

2
00:00:01.538 --> 00:00:02.651
This isn't free.

3
00:00:02.651 --> 00:00:05.766
It moves the cost from a
license line to staff time,

4
00:00:05.766 --> 00:00:09.413
including retesting every time
the platform is upgraded.

5
00:00:09.413 --> 00:00:12.776
It doesn't replace a full
identity-governance product,

6
00:00:12.776 --> 00:00:16.812
and if our needs grow, this buys
time rather than removing the need.

7
00:00:16.812 --> 00:00:21.308
Review is only as good as the
reviewer, and AI can produce confident,

8
00:00:21.308 --> 00:00:26.212
wrong code, so small changes and a
reviewer's right to say no really matter.

9
00:00:26.212 --> 00:00:30.183
The federal AI policy and the NIST
guidance are both still moving,

10
00:00:30.183 --> 00:00:31.874
so we'll need to recheck them.

11
00:00:31.874 --> 00:00:35.051
And the developer sandbox
belongs to the vendor,

12
00:00:35.051 --> 00:00:38.690
outside our boundary, so it
only ever holds made-up data.
